# Trivy ignore policy (Program 15 Phase 3). Rules:
#   - every entry carries the evidence for WHY it is ignored and an owner/date;
#   - entries are revisited when the referenced work item lands — an ignore
#     with a stale justification gets deleted, loudly breaking the scan.

# DS-0002 (HIGH): "Specify at least 1 USER command" — docker/postgres/Dockerfile.
# The pinned upstream entrypoint starts as root only to repair bind/named-volume
# ownership and migrate numeric UIDs, then directly re-execs itself as postgres
# through su-exec before initdb or the server runs. A global USER postgres would
# break that first-boot contract. This is an IaC shape exception, not a package-
# vulnerability exception. The pre-chown marker is a recoverability fence, not
# a security attestation. Revalidated for the Alpine lineage on 2026-08-30.
DS-0002
